==Usage== <!--T:46-->

<!--T:6-->
# Select a single sketch or one or more faces from the Body.
# There are several ways to invoke the tool:
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:PartDesign_Pocket.svg|16px]] [[PartDesign_Pocket|Pocket]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Part Design → Subtractive Features → [[Image:PartDesign_Pocket.svg|16px]] Pocket}} option from the menu.
# The task panel opens.
# Set the parameters, see [[#Options|Options]] below. {{Version|1.1}}: If the {{MenuCommand|Show interactive draggers when editing features}} [[PartDesign_Preferences#General|preference]] is selected (default), length and taper angle parameters can be adjusted with interactive gizmos in the [[3D_View|3D View]].
# Press the {{Button|OK}} button to close the task panel and finish the tool.

==Options== <!--T:3-->

<!--T:47-->
When creating a pocket, or after double-clicking an existing pocket in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]], the task panel opens. It offers the following settings:

<!--T:48-->
[[Image:PartDesign_Pocket_Taskpanel.png|frame]]

=== Start === <!--T:96-->

<!--T:97-->
Sets where the pocket begins. By default the pocket starts at the sketch or face used as its profile. {{Version|26.3}}
* '''Profile plane''' (default): the pocket starts directly at the profile's sketch plane or face.
* '''Offset''': the pocket starts at a numeric distance from the profile, entered in the '''Start Offset''' field.
* '''Reference''': the pocket starts at a face, [[Part_DatumPlane|datum plane]], or sketch selected with the {{Button|Pick Reference}} button.

<!--T:98-->
This is useful to create multiple features from a single master sketch without needing separate offset planes for each one.

===Direction=== <!--T:101-->

<!--T:102-->
You can select how the pocket is created:
* '''One sided''': the pocket extends on one side of the face.
* '''Two sided''': the pocket extends on both sides of the face. Two sub-menus (Side 1 and Side 2) appear to define the pocket for each side.
* '''Symmetric''': the pocket is symmetrical with respect to the original face.

===Type=== <!--T:29-->

<!--T:44-->
Type offers five different ways of specifying the length of the pocket:

====Dimension==== <!--T:49-->

<!--T:7-->
Enter a numeric value for the '''Length''' of the pocket. With the '''Direction''' option '''Symmetric''' the pocket will extend half the given length to either side of the sketch or face.

====Through all==== <!--T:50-->

<!--T:51-->
The pocket will extend up to the last face of the support it encounters in its direction. Note that for technical reasons, ''Through All'' is actually a 10 meter deep pocket. If you need deeper pockets, use the type '''Dimension'''.

====To first==== <!--T:52-->

<!--T:53-->
The pocket will extend up to the first face of the support it encounters in its direction.

====Up to face==== <!--T:54-->

<!--T:13-->
The pocket will extend up to a face. Press the {{Button|Select Face}} button and select a face or a [[Part_DatumPlane|datum plane]] from the Body.

====Up to shape==== <!--T:93-->

<!--T:94-->
{{Version|1.0}}: The pocket will extend up to the selected shape. Optionally press the {{Button|Select Shape}} button and select a shape. Leave the '''Select all faces''' checkbox enabled or disable it, press the {{Button|Select}} button and select the faces up to which the pocket should be created.

=== Offset to face === <!--T:59-->

<!--T:60-->
Offset from face at which the pocket will end. This option is only available if '''Type''' is '''To first''' or '''Up to face'''.

===Length=== <!--T:57-->

<!--T:58-->
Defines the length of the pocket. This option is only available if '''Type''' is '''Dimension'''.

=== Taper angle === <!--T:77-->

<!--T:79-->
Tapers the pocket in the extrusion direction by the given angle. A positive angle means the outer pocket border gets wider. This option is only available if '''Type''' is '''Dimension'''.

=== Reversed === <!--T:72-->

<!--T:73-->
Reverses the direction of the pocket.

=== Direction/edge === <!--T:63-->

<!--T:64-->
You can select the direction of the extrusion:

<!--T:65-->
* '''Sketch normal''' or '''Face normal:''' The sketch or face is extruded in the opposite direction of its normal. If you have selected several sketches or faces to be extruded, the normal of the first one will be used.
* '''Select reference…:''' The sketch or face is extruded in the opposite direction of a straight edge or a [[Part_DatumLine|datum line]] selected from the Body.
* '''Custom direction:''' The sketch or face is extruded in the direction of the specified vector.

=== Length along sketch normal === <!--T:68-->

<!--T:69-->
Uncheck this option to measure along the specified direction. This option is not available if '''Direction/edge''' is '''Sketch normal''' or '''Face normal'''.

===Operation=== <!--T:103-->

<!--T:104-->
Sets the boolean operation used to combine the pocket with the base solid. {{Version|26.3}}
* '''Subtraction''' (default): the pocket removes the extruded volume from the base solid, as in previous versions.
* '''Common''': the pocket keeps only the volume shared between the extruded profile and the base solid, discarding everything else. This is useful, for example, to trim a solid down to the intersection with a reference shape.

=== Recompute on change ===

This option should be checked if '''Show final result''' or '''Show preview overlay''' is checked.

=== Show final result ===

If checked the cumulative result of the previous features and the current operation is shown.

=== Show preview overlay ===

If checked the result of the current operation is shown as an overlay.

==Properties== <!--T:74-->

===Data=== <!--T:87-->

{{TitleProperty|Compatibility}}

* {{PropertyData|Use Legacy Taper Direction|Bool|Hidden}}: {{Version|26.3}}

<!--T:88-->
{{TitleProperty|Part Design}}

<!--T:89-->
* {{PropertyData|Operation|Enumeration}}: Sets the boolean operation used to combine the feature with the base solid (Subtraction, Common), see [[#Options|Options]]. {{Version|26.3}}
* {{PropertyData|Refine|Bool}}: True or false. Cleans up residual edges left after the operation. This property is initially set according to the user's settings (found in {{MenuCommand|Preferences → Part Design → General → Model Settings}}).
* {{PropertyData|Fuzzy Tolerance|FloatConstraint}}: {{Version|1.1}}

<!--T:90-->
{{TitleProperty|Pocket}}

<!--T:75-->
* {{PropertyData|Side Type|Enumeration}}: The options are: {{Value|One side}}, {{Value|Two sides}} and {{Value|Symmetric}}, see [[#Options|Options]]. {{Version|1.1}}
* {{PropertyData|Use Custom Vector|Bool}}: If checked, the pocket direction is based on the {{PropertyData|Direction}} vector instead of the {{PropertyData|Reference Axis}}.
* {{PropertyData|Direction|Vector}}: Vector of the pocket direction if {{PropertyData|Use Custom Vector}} is used.
* {{PropertyData|Reference Axis|LinkSub}}: The sketch normal, or an edge or datum line from the body.
* {{PropertyData|Along Sketch Normal|Bool}}: If checked, the pocket length is measured along the sketch normal. Otherwise it is measured along the {{PropertyData|Direction}} or {{PropertyData|Reference Axis}}.

{{TitleProperty|Side1}}

* {{PropertyData|Type|Enumeration}}: Defines how the pocket will be extruded, see [[#Options|Options]].
* {{PropertyData|Length|Length}}: Defines the length of the pocket, see [[#Options|Options]].
* {{PropertyData|Up To Face|LinkSub}}: A face the pocket will extrude up to, see [[#Options|Options]].
* {{PropertyData|Up To Shape|LinkSubList}}
* {{PropertyData|Offset|Length}}: Offset from face in which the pocket will end. This is only taken into account if the {{PropertyData|Type}} option '''UpToFirst''' or '''UpToFace''' is used.
* {{PropertyData|Taper Angle|Angle}}

{{TitleProperty|Side2}}

The properties in this group are only editable if {{PropertyData|Side Type}} is '''Two sides''', see [[#Options|Options]]. See the '''Side1''' group for more information about the properties.

* {{PropertyData|Type2|Enumeration}}: {{Version|1.1}}
* {{PropertyData|Length2|Length}}
* {{PropertyData|Up To Face2|LinkSub}}: {{Version|1.1}}
* {{PropertyData|Up To Shape2|LinkSubList}}: {{Version|1.1}}
* {{PropertyData|Offset2|Length}}: {{Version|1.1}}
* {{PropertyData|Taper Angle2|Angle}}

<!--T:91-->
{{TitleProperty|Sketch Based}}

<!--T:92-->
* {{PropertyData|Profile|LinkSub}}
* {{PropertyData|Midplane|Bool}}
* {{PropertyData|Reversed|Bool}}
* {{PropertyData|Allow Multi Face|Bool}}

<!--T:99-->
{{TitleProperty|Start}}

<!--T:100-->
* {{PropertyData|Start Type|Enumeration}}: Sets how the pocket start is defined (Profile plane, Offset, Reference), see [[#Options|Options]]. {{Version|26.3}}
* {{PropertyData|Start Offset|Length}}: Distance between the profile and the start of the pocket. Not used if {{PropertyData|Start Type}} is '''Profile plane'''. {{Version|26.3}}
* {{PropertyData|Start Reference|LinkSub}}: A face, plane, or sketch the pocket starts from. Only used if {{PropertyData|Start Type}} is '''Reference'''. {{Version|26.3}}

==Limitations== <!--T:76-->

<!--T:4-->
* Use the type '''Dimension''' or '''Through All''' wherever possible because the other types sometimes give trouble when they are being patterned.
* Other than that, the pocket feature has the same [[PartDesign_Pad#Limitations|limitations]] as the Pad feature.


